From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Domenico D'Arrigo <d.darrigo@outlook.it>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 10:13:34 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] sb/intel/lynxpoint: An ME halted on purpose is not an error

intel_me_path() took the error path whenever the MBP was not ready, so
an ME halted on purpose (the AltMeDisable bit of me_cleaner -S) logged
"mbp is not ready!" at BIOS_CRIT and a Management Engine error event at
every boot: 33 errors in 32 boots in the event log of a ThinkPad W541,
whose ME stops in its bring-up (operation mode 2, error code 0,
progress code 1) before it makes the MBP. A real error of the ME looked
the same.

Without an error code or a bad partition table, in debug or disabled
mode, the missing MBP is part of the disable path: say so at BIOS_INFO
and keep that path. The event log still records it (any path but the
normal one), with the extended data.

TEST=Builds for the W541 (mrc and nri). Remains for the hardware test:
a boot of the W541 logs "Management Engine disabled" (tools/elog.py)
instead of an error, and no "mbp is not ready".

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/southbridge/intel/lynxpoint/me.c | 15 +++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/southbridge/intel/lynxpoint/me.c b/src/southbridge/intel/lynxpoint/me.c
index 1a6de29b2c..0d1bac390a 100644
--- a/src/southbridge/intel/lynxpoint/me.c
+++ b/src/southbridge/intel/lynxpoint/me.c
@@ -687,8 +687,19 @@ static enum me_bios_path intel_me_path(struct device *dev)
 	if (hfs.error_code || hfs.fpt_bad)
 		path = ME_ERROR_BIOS_PATH;
 
-	/* Check if the MBP is ready */
-	if (!hfs2.mbp_rdy) {
+	/*
+	 * Check if the MBP is ready. An ME halted on purpose, in debug or
+	 * disabled mode without an error code (AltMeDisable, me_cleaner -S),
+	 * stops in its bring-up before it makes the MBP: that is its disable
+	 * path, not an error
+	 */
+	const bool halted = (hfs.operation_mode == ME_HFS_MODE_DEBUG ||
+			     hfs.operation_mode == ME_HFS_MODE_DIS) &&
+			    !hfs.error_code && !hfs.fpt_bad;
+	if (!hfs2.mbp_rdy && halted) {
+		printk(BIOS_INFO, "%s: ME halted in mode %u, no MBP\n", __func__,
+		       hfs.operation_mode);
+	} else if (!hfs2.mbp_rdy) {
 		printk(BIOS_CRIT, "%s: mbp is not ready!\n",
 		       __func__);
 		path = ME_ERROR_BIOS_PATH;
-- 
